; Fictional zone for example.com in master-file format (as BIND, Windows DNS or a zone transfer writes it).
; Same planted problems as records.csv, plus a DNSSEC signature next to a CNAME, which is not a conflict.
$ORIGIN example.com.
$TTL 3600
@           IN  SOA  ns1.example.com. hostmaster.example.com. (
                     2026111801 ; serial
                     7200 3600 1209600 3600 )
@           IN  NS     ns1.example.com.
@           IN  A      203.0.113.10
www         IN  CNAME  @
www         IN  RRSIG  CNAME 13 3 3600 20261201000000 20261118000000 12345 example.com. c2lnbmF0dXJl
shop        IN  CNAME  example-shop.azurewebsites.net.
docs        IN  CNAME  example-docs.github.io.
promo2024   IN  CNAME  promo2024-example.s3-website-us-east-1.amazonaws.com.
intranet    IN  A      10.20.0.15
legacy      IN  A      198.51.100.77
mail        IN  A      203.0.113.25
mail        IN  A      203.0.113.25
status  30  IN  CNAME  status-page.example.net.
status      IN  TXT    "verification=abc123; kept in quotes"
*.preview   IN  A      203.0.113.40
api 1209600 IN  A      203.0.113.30
ns1         IN  A      203.0.113.53
